  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>kg</mi></math> is connected to a spring of unknown spring constant k. It is compressed to a distance&nbsp;<math><mi>x</mi> </math> from its equilibrium position and released from rest. After approaching half the distance <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> from the equilibrium position, it hits another block and comes to rest momentarily, while the other block moves with velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The total initial energy of the spring is:",
